# === Warrior Bootstrap (Trading 212-like, avec backtesting/screener/watchlist & garde-fous) ===

## 1) Objectif du projet

Fournir une plateforme de trading propriétaire (frontend + backend) qui offre toutes les fonctionnalités essentielles de Trading212 / TradingView : charting professionnel, backtesting robuste, screener riche, profil d'actif (par id) avec analyse IA en temps réel, watchlists, news & calendrier économique, et scoring multi-dimensionnel (pentagone). Tout doit être typer (TypeScript) et prêt à être copié dans Cursor.

### Principes non négociables
- Conception modulaire et testable
- Types stricts (TypeScript strict: true)
- Observabilité (logs structurés, traces, métriques)
- Sécurité (chiffrement des clés, least privilege)
- Traçabilité des décisions IA (provenance + score de confiance)

## 2) Vue d'ensemble fonctionnelle — Features à ajouter/affiner
- Charting (ticks, intraday, multi-plot, indicators, drawing tools, save templates)
- Backtesting (historiques, monte-carlo, walk-forward, slippage, commissions)
- Screener (multi-filters, custom scripts, indicators, alerts)
- Recherche & profil par ID (fiches complètes, ratio, news, analyst notes, IA)
- Watchlist en temps réel (price + sentiment + news feed + alerts)
- Sentiment Analysis (news stream, social, calendar events)
- Calendar économique (filtres par pays / importance / impact)
- Pentagon scoring (5 axes, radar visualization, historical trend)
- Alert Engine (user rules + IA rules + webhook actions)
- Simulation / Paper trading + Live trading adapters (Alpaca, Polygon)
- Role-based UI: user, analyst, admin, dev

## 3) Architecture technique (haut niveau)

**Front-end**: Next.js (app router), React + TypeScript, Tailwind, Zustand/React Query for state + WebSocket handling

**Charting**: TradingView Charting Library (commercial) ou lightweight-charts pour la base + custom wrapper

**Back-end**: Node.js (NestJS/Express) en TypeScript

**Realtime**: WebSocket gateway (ws / uWebSockets) + Redis Pub/Sub

**Data pipeline**: Ingestion (WebSocket/API) → Kafka/Redis Streams → Worker cluster (Python/Node) → TimescaleDB / ClickHouse

**ML / NLP**: Python microservices (FastAPI) pour modèles NLP, inference (FinBERT, transformers), vector DB (Milvus / Pinecone)

**DBs**:
- Time-series: TimescaleDB (Postgres) ou ClickHouse
- OLTP: PostgreSQL
- Cache: Redis
- Vector embeddings: Milvus/Pinecone

**Storage**: S3 for snapshots and tick archives

**Observability**: OpenTelemetry + Prometheus + Grafana + Sentry

**Deployment**: Kubernetes (EKS/GKE) + CI (GitHub Actions)

## 4) Schémas d'API et contrats (à copier)

### 4.1 Format Watchlist (POST /api/watchlists)
```json
{
  "id": "wl_123",
  "name": "Tech Morning",
  "ownerId": "user_456",
  "items": [
    {"symbol":"AAPL","source":"NASDAQ","addedAt":"2025-09-01T08:00:00Z"},
    {"symbol":"TSLA","source":"NASDAQ","addedAt":"2025-09-01T08:01:00Z"}
  ],
  "realtime": true,
  "sentimentEnabled": true
}
```

### 4.2 Format Backtest request (POST /api/backtests)
```json
{
  "id":"bt_001",
  "userId":"user_456",
  "symbol":"AAPL",
  "start":"2020-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "end":"2024-12-31T23:59:59Z",
  "initialCapital":100000,
  "commission":0.001,
  "slippage":0.001,
  "strategy":{
    "type":"script",
    "language":"pine-like",
    "script":"ema(20) cross ema(50)"
  },
  "metrics":["sharpe","max_drawdown","annual_return"]
}
```

### 4.3 Format Screener query
```json
{
  "queryId":"sc_001",
  "filters":[
    {"field":"marketCap","op":">=","value":1000000000},
    {"field":"rsi","op":"<","value":30}
  ],
  "sort":[{"field":"volume","dir":"desc"}],
  "limit":200
}
```

### 4.4 Format Alert rule
```json
{
  "id":"alert_001",
  "ownerId":"user_123",
  "type":"price|strategy|sentiment|calendar",
  "payload":{ /* dépend du type */ },
  "actions": [{"type":"webhook","url":"https://..."}],
  "enabled":true,
  "createdAt":"2025-09-01T09:00:00Z"
}
```

## 5) Charting — exigences détaillées

### Objectif
Offrir un chart autant pro que TradingView : multi-timeframe, indicators, drawing tools, snapshots, fast pan/zoom, multi-series, OHLC + Ticks, study templates.

### Recommandations d'intégration
- Option A (si budget): TradingView Charting Library (pro) — meilleur out-of-the-box.
- Option B (open): lightweight-charts (TradingView OSS) + react-stockcharts pour features avancées.

### Fonctionnalités minimales à implémenter
- OHLC + Volume + Ticks
- Indicators: SMA, EMA, MACD, RSI, Bollinger
- Drawing tools: trendline, fib retracement, text, vertical/horizontal lines
- Multi-pane layout (indicators in separate panes)
- Template saving/loading per user
- Hotkeys & keyboard accessibility
- High performance for 10k+ ticks
- Export (PNG/SVG/CSV)

### API pour charting (web socket + REST)
- REST: /api/ohlc?symbol=AAPL&period=1m&start=...&end=...
- WS: wss://realtime.example.com/ticks?symbols=AAPL,TSLA — events: tick, snapshot, ohlc_update

### Data contracts (example tick event)
```json
{ "type":"tick", "symbol":"AAPL", "ts":"2025-09-18T08:04:00Z", "price":171.23, "size":100 }
```

## 6) Backtesting — design & API

### Principes
- Reproductibilité: chaque backtest doit stocker seeds, version du moteur, dataset hash
- Réalisme: slippage, commission, latency emulation
- Performance: workers en parallel (partition par symbol/date)

### Moteurs recommandés
- Python: vectorbt (rapide, numpy-driven), backtrader (mature), zipline (legacy)
- JS: backtesting.js (simple), mais heavy compute => Python conseillé

### Inputs/Outputs
- Input: stratégie (script ou config), univers, cash, fees
- Output: trades log, equity curve (timestamps), metrics, monte-carlo results, trade-by-trade P&L

## 7) Screener & Research

### Capacités
- Requête multi-filtres (financials, technicals, fundamentals, sentiment)
- Scripts custom (mini-language type PineScript-lite)
- Persisted screens + scheduling (run every X minutes)
- Export CSV & direct add-to-watchlist

### Data sources recommandées
- Finnhub, Polygon, IEX Cloud, Alpha Vantage (fundamentals), Morningstar (si licence)

## 8) Watchlist & Sentiment

### Watchlist
- Real-time price feed, last N news, IA summary and confidence, indicators snapshot
- Actions: add/remove, pin, set alerts, annotate

### Sentiment pipeline
1. Sources: NewsAPI, Twitter (X) stream (filtered), Reddit subreddits (optional), Stocktwits
2. Preprocess: language detection, dedup, timestamp normalization
3. NLP models: FinBERT or DistilBERT fine-tuned + VADER for lexicon baseline
4. Signals: polarity [-1..1], subject (earnings, guidance, macro), intensity, confidence
5. Store: time-series sentiment per symbol (per minute/hour/day)

### Calendar
- Ingest economic calendars (TradingEconomics, Investing.com API) → map to symbol/country → show importance (low/med/high)
- Allow linking calendar events to watchlist symbols

## 9) Pentagon scoring (Investing Warriors style)

### Dimensions (exemple)
1. Momentum
2. Volatility
3. Fundamentals
4. Sentiment
5. Risk (liquidity, drawdown)

### Calcul:
- Normaliser chaque métrique en 0..100
- Score pentagone = vecteur [d1..d5]
- Stocker historique pour affichage radar et évolution

### Endpoint prototype
GET /api/scores/pentagon?symbol=AAPL&period=30d

## 10) Alertes IA — charte et métadonnées

### Règles pour alertes générées par IA
- Toute alerte AI doit inclure: explainability (short rationale), confidence (0..1), sources (list), modelVersion, timestamp
- Default: IA alerts are suggestions. Require user opt-in to auto-execute.

### Exemple d'alerte IA
```json
{
  "id":"ia_alert_001",
  "symbol":"AAPL",
  "type":"sentiment_shift",
  "confidence":0.82,
  "explain":"Augmentation significative des mentions négatives après publication de guidance",
  "sources":["news:nytimes:2025-09-18:...","twitter:..."],
  "model":"finbert-v1",
  "createdAt":"2025-09-18T09:00:00Z"
}
```

### Garde-fous humains
- Tag autoExecute:false par défaut pour IA
- Historique des alertes et possibilité d'audit
- Rate-limiting des alertes IA pour éviter spam

## 11) Gestion des erreurs & Observabilité

### Error handling
- Use typed error classes (e.g., APIError {code, message, retriable, meta})
- Central error middleware (capturer et normaliser)
- Circuit-breaker patterns (Opossum for Node)
- Retry with exponential backoff (axios-retry / backoff libs)

### Monitoring & Logs
- Traces: OpenTelemetry
- Errors: Sentry
- Metrics: Prometheus
- Dashboards: Grafana

## 12) Sécurité & gestion des clés
- Store secrets in KMS (AWS KMS / HashiCorp Vault)
- Never store API keys in repo. Use encrypted env in deploy and secure local dev .env.local.example
- Per-user tokenization for broker keys; never keep plaintext
- Scopes: separate read-only vs trading keys
- Rate-limit and IP allowlists

## 13) Tests & CI/CD
- Unit tests: Jest (TS), PyTest for Python
- Integration: Playwright for E2E
- Backtest reproducibility tests: snapshot results hash
- CI: GitHub Actions — run lint, tests, build, deploy to staging

